Hello Filipe,
fist of all congratulations for your fantastic work!
I've tried FieldimageR with my data (UAV of maize plots of which I need plant counting), and in order to improve soil removal I'm trying to use the BGI, exactly as you show in the tutorial. It works fine producing a nice mask.
However, when I apply fieldCount it produces the following error:
Error in distmap(mask) : 'x' shouldn't contain any NAs

Otherwise when I used the tutorial example for soil removal (i.e. using Hue) it had worked fine (though I wasn't satisfied with the counting results)...
Any hint for solving this issue?
Thanks a lot
Cheers
Raffaele

